text:
{
  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "106",
  "quote": "If the lawful rent increases after a tenant has paid a rent deposit, the landlord may require the tenant to pay an additional amount to increase the rent deposit up to the amount permitted by subsection (2).",
  "reason": "Because the rent is payable monthly, the maximum permitted rent deposit under subsection 106(2) is one month's rent. Subsection 106(3) explicitly allows the landlord to require the tenant to pay an additional amount to bring the rent deposit up to the new monthly rent when the rent is lawfully increased."
}

